.TH PROFILE-LINT 1 "2026-11-05" "pv-suite 0.4.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
profile-lint \- lint the pv-suite device profiles
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B profile-lint.py
.RI [ FILE ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lints the pv-suite device-profile JSON files \(em the shared register maps
consumed by
.BR modbus-fake-inverter (1),
.BR modbus-cache (1)
and
.BR modbus-scraper (1).
Without arguments it lints every \fBprofiles/profiles/*.json\fR in the
suite checkout; named files win.
.PP
The checks: valid JSON and the top-level shape; a non-empty
\fBdescription\fR; the required keys and their family order (\fBname\fR
\(-> \fBregister\fR \-> \fBtype\fR \-> \fBscale\fR \-> \fBdesc\fR); the
register bounds (0\(en65536 minus the type width); the valid types
(\fBi16/u16/i32/u32\fR); \fBfc\fR \(is {3, 4}; a numeric \fBttl\fR \(>= 0;
terse-ASCII \fBdesc\fRs; the mappings against a profile register word;
the write acl gate (\fBacl\fR/\fBwrite\fR: an optional terse-ASCII
\fBdesc\fR and the ordered \fBrules\fR list, one
\fB{"type": "allow"|"deny", "range": ...}\fR object per rule \(em
\fBSTART:COUNT\fR matchers \(em bare or listed \(em or the bare word
\fBany\fR, bounds checked, a terse-ASCII \fBdesc\fR
per rule); duplicate
names; same-fc register overlaps. One issue per line, exit non-zero on
the first failure.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
every file lints clean.
.TP
.B 1
an invalid file (the reason is printed).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR profile-format (1)
.PP
\fBprofiles/README.md\fR in the suite checkout \(em the profile format.
